course: dictionary
lesson: 3784
title: Footballer and the word family of play
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A footballer is a person who plays football, especially as a job. You can find the meaning by splitting the word: football is the game, and the ending -er means a person who does it. A teacher teaches and a footballer plays football.
explain: Read the context. «Zara in Johannesburg met a famous footballer at the airport and showed a blurry photo of a tall man's back.» The words famous and photo tell you the footballer is well known. The word footballer tells you what the man does: he plays football.
explain: Other words can sit next to footballer. «Professional footballer» means someone who is paid to play. «Young footballer» means a child who plays. A footballer also wears kit at matches, so the word kit is a clue too.
fact: A footballer is a person who plays football, especially as a job.
fact: «Professional footballer» means a footballer who is paid to play.
fact: The plural of footballer is footballers: one footballer, many footballers.
fact: In the UK, football means soccer. In the USA, Canada and parts of Australia, football can mean other games, so a footballer there may play American football or rugby league.
fact: Adverts often use famous footballers to make us feel happy, cool or grown-up, so always ask why the advert chose them.
exercise: «Zara met a famous footballer at the airport.» What is a footballer? | A kind of ball | *A person who plays football | A football pitch | A person who sells football tickets
exercise: What is the plural of footballer? | footballing | *footballers | footballer's | footballs
exercise: In the USA, what might football mean? | Cricket | *American football | Tennis | Only soccer, always
test: «Ads use famous footballers to sell things.» Why do adverts use famous footballers? | To show how to kick a ball | *To make people feel happy, cool or grown-up and want the product | To give people a free football | To make the advert shorter
test: What does «professional footballer» mean? | A referee who blows the whistle | A footballer who cannot play | A footballer who is seven years old | *A footballer who is paid to play
exam: In «a footballer has home kit and away kit», what does kit most likely mean? | A ticket for the match | A goal | *A set of team clothes | A football pitch
